  "notes": "Xiaomi Mi TV P1 43\" (MiTV-MOOQ2, codename croods, MediaTek), Android TV 11, firmware RTM4.220307.164.8238\nLatin America retail unit (L43M6), 1.7 GB RAM, Android low-RAM mode on. Same croods chassis as MiTV-MOOQ0.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mooq2/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mooq2/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED for user 0, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\nProvisional: applied in one session and reboot-checked; every package stayed disabled after reboot.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher. It is NOT in this list: launcher/build-and-install.sh\ndisables it after com.gathin.tvhome is installed and verified as Home (default STOCK_LAUNCHER detection works).\nOnly com.android.tv.settings and the stock launcher claim HOME on this firmware; setupwraith does not, so\nit stays enabled and the saved Wi-Fi network is untouched.\n\nKept deliberately, checked with `dumpsys package`:\ncom.mitv.overseaservice                        hosts netflixService (the Netflix key), as on MOSR4\ncom.xiaomi.android.tvsetup.partnercustomizer   holds BleRcActivity, the Bluetooth remote pairing\ncom.xiaomi.tvqs.overseas                       TV quick-settings receivers\ncom.mediatek.tvinput, com.mediatek.wwtv.tvcenter, mitv.service, com.mediatek.tv.service   HDMI 1-3, AV, tuner\ncom.xiaomi.mitv.updateservice                  firmware updates, kept by owner's choice\n\nBefore disabling com.mitv.dream and com.google.android.backdrop, point the screensaver elsewhere:\nsettings put secure screensaver_components com.gathin.tvhome/.ClockDream\n\nTested after the debloat: launcher Inputs menu lists HDMI 1-3, AV and Live TV; Netflix, YouTube, Prime Video\nand Max launch; Chromecast, Mi Cast/Miracast and the Bluetooth remote still work.\n---- Xiaomi and Google telemetry ----",
